Verse 1:
[Ab]Jesus, Savior, [Db]pilot [Ab]me
Over [Db]life’s tem[Eb7]pestuous [Ab]sea;
[Eb7]Unknown waves before me [Ab]roll,
[Eb7]Hiding rock and treacherous [Ab]shoal.
[Ab]Chart and compass [Db]come from [Ab]Thee;
Jesus, [Db]Savior, [Eb7]pilot [Ab]me.

Verse 2:
[Ab]As a [Db]mother stills [Ab]her child,
[Db]thou canst [Eb7]hush the [Ab]ocean wild;
[Eb7]boisterous waves [Ab]obey thy will,
[Eb7]when thou sayest [Ab]to them, "Be still!"
[Ab]Wondrous [Db]sovreign of [Ab]the sea,
[Db]Jesus, [Eb7]Savior, [Ab]pilot me.

Verse 3:
[Ab]When at [Db]last I [Ab]near the shore,
[Db]and [Eb7]the fearful [Ab]breakers roar
[Eb7]'twixt me and [Ab]the peaceful rest,
[Eb7]then, while leaning [Ab]on thy breast,
[Ab]may I [Db]hear thee [Ab]say to me,
[Db]"Fear not, [Eb7]I will [Ab]pilot thee.
